    "author": "Bruce Allen Dickey",
    "description": "Reproduction study — inspired by Lautus Notation (Bruce Allen Dickey, 2011). Minor-third 4-line staff at G#/B/D/F with the F line bold; uniform solid oval noteheads. In place of a clef a large octave numeral is shown, exercised here in the platform's register-label (text) clef mode. Dickey's stem-system duration devices (half = half-height neighbour stem, whole = double stem, breve = triple stem, stem-like rests) need the unimplemented stem enhancement (E3) and are documented as a deviation. The published numeral-clef glyph shape is deferred as an asset. Built from the public gallery description/image; not endorsed by or derived from the original.",
